# App screenshots are source material, not source code.
#
# They have to live under public/ because the canvas renders them with a plain
# <img src="/screenshots/...">, and html-to-image can only snapshot same-origin
# images — a remote URL taints the canvas and the export comes out blank. That
# is a serving requirement, not a versioning one: keep the files on disk here,
# just don't publish them.
#
# What stays tracked is the part worth versioning: each folder's ASSETS.md
# (what a deck expects, and what's still missing) and projects/<app>.json (the
# deck itself, which references these paths). A fresh clone renders empty
# device screens until you drop the real captures back in.
public/screenshots/**/*.png
public/screenshots/**/*.jpg
public/screenshots/**/*.jpeg
public/screenshots/**/*.webp

# Icons are the exception: already public on the stores, a few KB, and the
# feature-graphic layout can't render without one.
!public/screenshots/*/app-icon.png
